-- title:
--   Inertia is trivial on the Gauss branch: second row
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'\neq 0$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ for $\{q\ell\}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. Let $K\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with $A\to K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$; let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$. Let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$, and form the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the spectra of the finite and infinite chart algebras (the integral closures of $A[j]$, resp. its counterpart, in $K$). Let $z\in\mathfrak X$ be a point at which the image $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ followed by the germ map lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A)$, $\mathcal A$ the finite chart algebra, lie over $z$, and assume $y$ is supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:\mathcal A\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma:A\to W$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, let $u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ be units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, put $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\,C(\sigma\varpi)v-fu\,)$ with quotient map $\mathrm{mkS}$, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S$. Write $\mathrm{germY}:\mathcal A\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ for the germ at $z$ through the finite chart and $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map to the completion. Assume the anchoring clause: for every prime $P$ of $S$ that omits at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, contains $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and contains $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0+h)$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a\in\mathcal A$, one has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)\in e^{-1}(P)$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$. The conclusion: let $\sigma_L$ be a ring automorphism of $L$ and $\sigma_A$ one of $A$ compatible with it, with $\sigma_A a-a\in\mathfrak m_A$ for all $a\in A$; let $\tau$ be a ring automorphism of $K$ acting on Laurent series coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$ and preserving $\mathcal A$; let $\theta$ be a ring automorphism of $S$ with $\theta(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)))=e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\tau a)))$ for all $a\in\mathcal A$; and let $M\in M_2(W)$ satisfy $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_j))\equiv \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_i M_{ij}X_i\big)$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$. Then $M_{10}\in\mathfrak m_W$ and $M_{11}-1\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   This is the row of the linear-part computation saying that an automorphism of the Drinfeld-type local chart coming from an inertial automorphism of $K$ over the residue data acts trivially, to first order modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, on the branch $X_0=0$ anchored at the cusp. It feeds the determination of the inertia action on the linear part of the chart at a supersingular point of the full-level integral model.
